# ------------------------------------------------------------------ simple reading for the wheels (plain English, short sentences)
READING.extend("""I am a student. I go to school every day. My school is near my house. I walk to school with my friends.
She has a small dog. The dog is brown and white. It likes to run in the park. Every morning she gives it water and food.
We eat breakfast at seven o'clock. I like bread, eggs and milk. My mother makes tea for the family.
The sun is bright today. The sky is blue and the birds are singing. It is a good day to walk outside.
He works in a big office. He starts work at nine and finishes at five. After work he reads a book or watches a film.
My brother plays football on Saturday. His team is very good. They train three times a week.
It is raining. Please take an umbrella. The streets are wet and the air is cool.
The shop is open from morning to night. You can buy fruit, vegetables, bread and milk there. The shop keeper is kind.
I like to read books. A good book can take you to another place. Reading every day helps you learn new words.
Tom and Anna are friends. They talk on the phone after school. They help each other with homework.
Can you help me, please? I would like a glass of water. Thank you very much. You are welcome.
What is your name? My name is Sara. Where do you live? I live in a small town near the sea.
Yesterday we went to the market. We bought apples, rice and eggs. Then we came home and cooked dinner.
Tomorrow I will visit my grandmother. She lives far away, so I will take a train. I will bring her some flowers.
The children are playing in the garden. They run, jump and laugh. Their mother watches them from the window.
Winter is cold and summer is hot. In spring the flowers open. In autumn the leaves fall from the trees.
A teacher helps students to learn. A doctor helps sick people. A farmer grows food. A driver takes people from place to place.
He is tall and she is short. The red car is fast and the old bus is slow. The soup is hot and the juice is cold.
Please close the door. Open your books. Listen to the teacher. Write your name at the top of the page.
Do you like music? I like music very much. I listen to songs when I walk and when I cook.
My room is small but clean. There is a bed, a desk and a chair. On the desk there are books and a lamp.
Language is how people share ideas. We speak, write, read and listen. A new word each day makes a big difference.
Good morning, everyone. Today we will learn about nouns and verbs. A noun is a name. A verb is an action.
I am happy to meet you. How are you today? I am fine, thank you. Have a nice day.""".split("\n"))

